-- title:
--   Algebraic places accumulate at a non-cuspidal place of X₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and write $\bar{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. Let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` be the intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb Q}((q))$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull N` (itself the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by `divisorExpansions N`). A place of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ is a valuation subring of $F$, distinct from $F$, containing the image of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and a principal ideal ring. Let $v_0$ be such a place whose valuation subring contains the element of $F$ given by the coefficientwise image of `jq` $= q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the } j\text{-numerator series})$; let $\sigma\colon\bar{\mathbb Q}\to\mathbb C$ be a ring homomorphism, $S$ a finite set of places of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, and $Y$ a finite set of elements of $F$ all lying in the valuation subring of $v_0$. Then there is a sequence $(v_n)_{n\in\mathbb N}$ of places of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ with $v_n\notin S$ and $v_n\ne v_0$ for all $n$, such that each $y\in Y$ lies in the valuation subring of every $v_n$, satisfies $\mathrm{evalAt}_{v_n}(y)\ne 0$ for all $n$ whenever $y\ne 0$, and $\sigma(\mathrm{evalAt}_{v_n}(y))\to\sigma(\mathrm{evalAt}_{v_0}(y))$ as $n\to\infty$. Here `evalAt` sends an element of the valuation subring to the element of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ obtained from its residue class by a chosen inverse of the structure map $\bar{\mathbb Q}\to$ residue field, and sends elements outside the valuation subring to $0$.
--
--   This is the statement that the algebraic points of the modular curve $X_0(N)$, presented here through places of its function field over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$, accumulate at any given non-cuspidal point in the complex topology induced by an embedding $\sigma\colon\bar{\mathbb Q}\to\mathbb C$, convergence being tested against finitely many functions regular at that point, while avoiding a prescribed finite set of places. It is the interior counterpart of the corresponding accumulation statement at the cusp at infinity, and feeds [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_seq_tendsto_place`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_seq_tendsto_place).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_seq_place_tendsto_evalAt.lean

